# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context, so it never
# reaches the Docker daemon and can never end up in an image layer.

# The image builds only ./cmd/web (see Dockerfile).
#
# Version control metadata. Keeping .git out also means `go build` has no VCS to
# stamp, which is why the builder stage passes -buildvcs=false.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
.kiro

# Local build output and test artifacts
engine
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
*.log

# Runtime data. The runtime stage creates its own empty /app/storage.
storage

# Container and project docs
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
compose*.yml
README.md
LICENSE

# Tests are not needed to compile the binary
**/*_test.go

# Real environment files. Only .env.example is needed, and the runtime stage
# bakes it as /app/.env. Mount the real file at runtime
# (-v /path/to/.env:/app/.env:ro) so secrets never reach the Docker daemon.
.env
.env.test
